From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:14:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ilp32: parse the GNU property notes of ELF32 files

binfmt_ilp32.c builds fs/binfmt_elf.c for ELF32 files but kept the ELF64
ELF_GNU_PROPERTY_ALIGN of 8. The program properties of an ELF32 file are
4-byte aligned, so parse_elf_property() refused every ILP32 executable
or interpreter with a PT_GNU_PROPERTY segment with -ENOEXEC: for example
any program built with -mbranch-protection=bti, on every CPU, with or
without BTI.

Use ELF32_GNU_PROPERTY_ALIGN, as fs/compat_binfmt_elf.c does. ELF_COMPAT
stays 0: ILP32 runs AArch64 code, so arch_parse_elf_property() applies
GNU_PROPERTY_AARCH64_FEATURE_1_BTI as for LP64.

Tested on QEMU -cpu max and cortex-a35: an ILP32 program with a BTI
property note runs (it was refused with ENOEXEC before), and an indirect
call to a function without a BTI landing pad raises SIGILL with BTI
(-cpu max), as for the same LP64 program.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_ilp32.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_ilp32.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_ilp32.c
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@
 #define elf_note	elf32_note
 #define elf_addr_t	Elf32_Addr
 
+/* GNU property notes of ELF32 files are 4-byte aligned */
+#undef	ELF_GNU_PROPERTY_ALIGN
+#define ELF_GNU_PROPERTY_ALIGN	ELF32_GNU_PROPERTY_ALIGN
+
 /*
  * Some data types as stored in coredump.
  */
